 "title": "Sakura Sakura",
 "description": "The Japanese cherry-blossom song as Tokyo's music school first printed it in 1888, for 2 to 4 singers: the tune in its own five-note scale over soft held notes on \"oo\", like a koto's open strings, with no Western chords. Slow and calm, sung in Japanese (the words are shown in romaji).",
